{
  "info": {
    "name": "Umoja OAuth API",
    "description": "OAuth and auth-demo endpoints for Umoja API.\n\n## Setup\n- **Strapi v5**: When using the control-plane (Strapi), `client_id` must be the **documentId** (e.g. `clxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx`), not a numeric id. Run `npm run seed:oauth` in `apps/umoja-control-plane` and copy the printed **client_id (use in OAuth token requests)** into the environment variable `client_id`.\n- Set `includeControllers: true` in AuthModule for /oauth/token and /oauth/authorize.\n\n## Test scenarios (positive)\n- **API Key**: Create client/user with valid x-api-key → 201; Admin with valid x-api-key → 200; Session with valid Basic auth → 200.\n- **OAuth Token**: Client credentials / Password / Refresh with valid credentials → 200, body has access_token and token_type Bearer.\n- **Protected**: Profile/Me with valid Bearer → 200, body has user; Profile Write with scope write → 200 or 403 if scope missing.\n- **Root**: GET / → 200.\n\n## Test scenarios (negative)\n- **Admin without x-api-key** → 401.\n- **Profile without Authorization** → 401.\n- **Profile with invalid Bearer** → 401.\n- **Token with wrong client_secret** → 401.\n- **Token with wrong password** → 401.\n- **Token with invalid refresh_token** → 401.\n- **Create Client without x-api-key** → 401.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "http://localhost:3000" },
    { "key": "api_key", "value": "umoja-api-key-demo" },
    { "key": "client_id", "value": "PASTE_DOCUMENT_ID_FROM_SEED_OUTPUT" },
    { "key": "client_secret", "value": "umoja-demo-secret" },
    { "key": "username", "value": "demo-user" },
    { "key": "password", "value": "demo-pass" },
    { "key": "access_token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "refresh_token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "redirect_uri", "value": "http://localhost:3000/callback" },
    { "key": "state", "value": "postman-state" },
    { "key": "authorization_code", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth (API Key)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create Client",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('Response has clientId and clientSecret', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('clientId');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('clientSecret');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.clientId).to.be.a('string');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.clientSecret).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Response has grants array', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('grants');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.grants).to.be.an('array');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "x-api-key", "value": "{{api_key}}", "type": "text" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json", "type": "text" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"postman-client\",\n  \"grants\": [\"password\", \"client_credentials\", \"refresh_token\"],\n  \"redirectUris\": [\"http://localhost:3000/callback\"],\n  \"scopes\": [\"read\"],\n  \"audiences\": [\"umoja-clients\"]\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/auth-demo/clients",
            "description": "Scenario: Valid x-api-key → 201, body has clientId, clientSecret, grants."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create User",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('Response has user with id and username', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('user');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.user).to.have.property('username');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.user.username).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "x-api-key", "value": "{{api_key}}", "type": "text" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json", "type": "text" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"postman-user\",\n  \"password\": \"postman-pass\",\n  \"scopes\": [\"read\", \"write\"]\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/auth-demo/users",
            "description": "Scenario: Valid x-api-key → 201, body has user with username."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Admin (API Key)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Response indicates API key valid', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('message');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.message).to.include('API key');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('role', 'admin');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "x-api-key", "value": "{{api_key}}", "type": "text" }],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/auth-demo/admin",
            "description": "Scenario: Valid x-api-key → 200, body has message and role admin."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Session (Basic Auth)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Response has user and Basic auth valid message', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('user');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('message');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.message).to.include('Basic');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "basic",
              "basic": [
                { "key": "username", "value": "{{username}}", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "password", "value": "{{password}}", "type": "string" }
              ]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/auth-demo/session",
            "description": "Scenario: Valid Basic auth (demo-user / demo-pass) → 200, body has user and message."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "OAuth Token",
      "description": "Run **Token - Password** first to obtain `refresh_token` (saved to environment). **Token - Refresh** requires that value; client_credentials does not return refresh_token.\n\nRecommended order: 1) Token - Client Credentials (optional), 2) Token - Password, 3) Token - Refresh.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Token - Client Credentials",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Response has access_token and token_type Bearer', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('access_token');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.access_token).to.be.a('string');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('token_type', 'Bearer');",
                  "});",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  if (json.access_token) pm.environment.set('access_token', json.access_token);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded", "type": "text" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                { "key": "grant_type", "value": "client_credentials" },
                { "key": "client_id", "value": "{{client_id}}" },
                { "key": "client_secret", "value": "{{client_secret}}" }
              ]
            },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/oauth/token",
            "description": "Scenario: Valid client_id (Strapi v5: use documentId from seed) + client_secret → 200, body has access_token and token_type Bearer."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Token - Password",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Response has access_token, refresh_token and token_type Bearer', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('access_token');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('refresh_token');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('token_type', 'Bearer');",
                  "});",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  if (json.access_token) pm.environment.set('access_token', json.access_token);",
                  "  if (json.refresh_token) pm.environment.set('refresh_token', json.refresh_token);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded", "type": "text" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                { "key": "grant_type", "value": "password" },
                { "key": "username", "value": "{{username}}" },
                { "key": "password", "value": "{{password}}" },
                { "key": "client_id", "value": "{{client_id}}" },
                { "key": "client_secret", "value": "{{client_secret}}" }
              ]
            },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/oauth/token",
            "description": "Scenario: Valid username + password + client_id (Strapi v5: documentId from seed) → 200, body has access_token and refresh_token."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Token - Refresh",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Response has access_token and token_type Bearer', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('access_token');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('token_type', 'Bearer');",
                  "});",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  if (json.access_token) pm.environment.set('access_token', json.access_token);",
                  "  if (json.refresh_token) pm.environment.set('refresh_token', json.refresh_token);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded", "type": "text" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                { "key": "grant_type", "value": "refresh_token" },
                { "key": "refresh_token", "value": "{{refresh_token}}" },
                { "key": "client_id", "value": "{{client_id}}" },
                { "key": "client_secret", "value": "{{client_secret}}" }
              ]
            },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/oauth/token",
            "description": "Scenario: Valid refresh_token + client_id → 200, new access_token (and new refresh_token). Use a refresh_token from **Token - Password** (saved to env); client_credentials does not issue refresh_token. Run Token - Password before this request."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "OAuth Authorization Code",
      "description": "Two-step flow: 1) **Authorize (get code)** – GET /oauth/authorize with Basic auth (resource owner). Server redirects (302) to redirect_uri with ?code=...&state=...; the Test script saves the code to `authorization_code`. 2) **Token - Authorization Code** – POST /oauth/token to exchange the code for access_token and refresh_token. Run Authorize first; ensure client has grant authorization_code and redirectUris includes {{redirect_uri}} (e.g. http://localhost:3000/callback).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Authorize (get code)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 302 Redirect', () => pm.response.to.have.status(302));",
                  "const loc = pm.response.headers.get('Location');",
                  "pm.test('Location has code and state', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(loc).to.be.a('string');",
                  "  pm.expect(loc).to.include('code=');",
                  "});",
                  "if (loc && loc.includes('code=')) {",
                  "  const match = loc.match(/code=([^&]+)/);",
                  "  if (match) pm.environment.set('authorization_code', decodeURIComponent(match[1]));",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "basic",
              "basic": [
                { "key": "username", "value": "{{username}}", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "password", "value": "{{password}}", "type": "string" }
              ]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/oauth/authorize?response_type=code&client_id={{client_id}}&redirect_uri={{redirect_uri}}&state={{state}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["oauth", "authorize"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "response_type", "value": "code" },
                { "key": "client_id", "value": "{{client_id}}" },
                { "key": "redirect_uri", "value": "{{redirect_uri}}" },
                { "key": "state", "value": "{{state}}" }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Scenario: Resource owner (Basic auth) requests authorization. Server responds 302 with Location: redirect_uri?code=...&state=...; Test script parses the code and saves it to authorization_code. Disable 'Automatically follow redirects' for this request (Request → Settings) so the 302 response is returned and the script can read the Location header. Client must have grant authorization_code and redirectUris including {{redirect_uri}} (e.g. http://localhost:3000/callback)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Token - Authorization Code",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Response has access_token, refresh_token and token_type Bearer', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('access_token');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('refresh_token');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('token_type', 'Bearer');",
                  "});",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  if (json.access_token) pm.environment.set('access_token', json.access_token);",
                  "  if (json.refresh_token) pm.environment.set('refresh_token', json.refresh_token);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded", "type": "text" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                { "key": "grant_type", "value": "authorization_code" },
                { "key": "code", "value": "{{authorization_code}}" },
                { "key": "redirect_uri", "value": "{{redirect_uri}}" },
                { "key": "client_id", "value": "{{client_id}}" },
                { "key": "client_secret", "value": "{{client_secret}}" }
              ]
            },
            "url": "{{base_url}}/oauth/token",
            "description": "Scenario: Exchange authorization code for tokens. Run **Authorize (get code)** first so authorization_code is set. redirect_uri must match the one used in the authorize step."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
